module j3.i18nplural
    The language and number rules behind `j3.i18n`: CLDR plural categories (`plural`) and locale number formats
    (`pushNum`, `pushReal`). Pure functions on a language code, usable on their own. Any thread.

fn langOf(name: string): string
    The language of a locale name: `pt-BR` and `pt_BR` give `pt`.
fn plural(lang: string, n: int, frac: bool): string
    The CLDR plural category (`zero`, `one`, `two`, `few`, `many`, `other`) of `n` in language `lang` (`en`, `ru`,
    `pt-BR`; an unknown language follows English). `frac` says the number has a visible fraction (1.5): `n` is its
    integer part. Covers en/de/nl/sv (one/other), fr/pt (0 and 1 are one), es/it, ru/uk, pl, ar, and ja/zh/ko/vi/th/id
    (other). The compact-number `many` of es/fr/it/pt (millions) is not implemented.
struct Split
    n: int
    frac: int
        Thousandths after the point, 0 to 999.
    neg: bool

fn split(v: f32): Split
fn pushNum(out: &Text, lang: string, n: int)
fn pushReal(out: &Text, lang: string, v: f32)
